    <node id="spatula">
      <data key="d0">spatula</data>
      <data key="d1">utensil</data>
      <data key="d2">"A kitchen utensil used for flipping or serving food."&lt;SEP&gt;A spatula is a versatile kitchen utensil primarily used for flipping or spreading food. It is commonly made from various materials and is available in multiple colors, including black. As a cooking tool, it serves not only for flipping but also for mixing and serving food, making it an essential item in any kitchen.&lt;SEP&gt;"black cooking utensil"</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"grasp;"move;"move";grasp";lift;move;place"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The spatula is a black cooking utensil located at the center of the table.&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is a black cooking utensil that serves as a valuable tool in various kitchen tasks, particularly in moving food items. In one instance, a user was tasked with relocating the spatula from the right counter to a receptacle on the left counter. However, confusion arose when the spatula was inadvertently left at the sink instead of being properly placed in its intended receptacle. Ultimately, despite the user's efforts to move the spatula, it remained grasped in their hand, exemplifying a moment of uncertainty regarding its use. The spatula is central to cooking activities and is typically positioned on the table, highlighting its importance in the kitchen setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The spatula is a kitchen tool intended for moving food items from one place to another.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-5b177bd9c702eeed3f097f492ce125d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-719948bd18c9bdf0dde1938e63ccd374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce436dad6d3dd09536a67a0309aab8e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c5b4e6c04f6766e6046e86be00b31f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-573ef3404f5628761757f187f5bdd463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e2325f019dbb8959a980621cfad27b</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d10">1772882130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="right counter">
      <data key="d0">right counter</data>
      <data key="d1">surface</data>
      <data key="d2">The right counter is a specific area in the kitchen designed as a flat, horizontal workspace primarily used for preparation or storage. Constructed from light brown wood with a polished finish, it enhances the kitchen's aesthetic appeal. This counter features a mounted robotic arm, which significantly aids in food preparation and various cooking tasks. Initially, it housed a spatula, underscoring its functional role in cooking activities. Additionally, the right counter is equipped with two cabinet doors, providing extra storage space for essential kitchen items.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">The "right counter" is referenced in a series of descriptions that primarily indicate "N/A" three times, suggesting a lack of specific details about its features or functions. However, it is noted that the right counter is located in the "upper right corner," which provides insight into its position or placement within a certain context. This detail is important for understanding the physical or graphical layout related to the right counter. Overall, while the available information is limited, it clearly states that the right counter is positioned in the upper right corner.</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The right counter is a prominent feature in the kitchen area, distinguished by its light brown wood finish and polished surface. It is situated in the upper right corner of the living space and serves multiple functional purposes, playing a significant role in various culinary tasks. Notably, the counter is equipped with a mounted robotic arm in its upper right corner, enhancing its utility for food preparation activities. 

The right counter is critical for organizing kitchen tasks, as it has been identified as the initial placement for a strawberry, highlighting its importance in cooking processes. Additionally, it was previously recorded as the incorrect location for a bowl, a detail that has since been corrected in the user's memory update. The counter is also where a spatula is commonly placed, and it has served as the final resting place for a sponge after task completion. Furthermore, it is mentioned that both the sponge and a ball were intended to be placed on the counter as part of the ongoing tasks, further demonstrating its multifunctional use within the kitchen and living area.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-6fa57c865be49ee5edbc8fad39548f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fc77f14a1677f08b51cf57e31a8b703&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b177bd9c702eeed3f097f492ce125d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd190f719d592d9b0f1509b77990754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-719948bd18c9bdf0dde1938e63ccd374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f6e8d68fdac39353f5a045b8d3c104b</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d10">1772792830</data>
