    <node id="left counter">
      <data key="d0">left counter</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A counter situated to the left, used for various tasks and holding objects."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surface or piece of furniture used in a kitchen or workspace."&lt;SEP&gt;The left counter is a flat, horizontal workspace primarily located in the kitchen. Positioned to the left of the right counter, it is characterized by a darker color and a matte finish, which enhances the overall aesthetic of the kitchen. This multifunctional counter serves as a designated area for food preparation and cooking activities, facilitating the use of kitchen tools such as spatulas. Often adorned with a bowl of fruits or vegetables, it adds both functionality and visual appeal to the space.

In addition to its culinary uses, the left counter provides versatility as it can also be utilized as a surface in the living area for placing or storing various objects, thus expanding its utility beyond just kitchen tasks. It features a left drawer that aids in the effective organization of kitchen items, as well as cabinets below that complement its design and increase the overall storage options available. Overall, the left counter is an essential piece of furniture, combining practicality with aesthetic charm in both kitchen and living spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"hold;"place;interact";organize";place;prepare</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The left counter is primarily characterized by its proximity to the center, making it "closer to the center." Other descriptions related to the left counter are marked as "N/A," indicating a lack of additional information available. Therefore, the most significant detail about the left counter is its position in relation to the center.</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The left counter is a darker kitchen surface strategically located closer to the center of the living area, playing a crucial role in organizing kitchen tasks and food preparation. It is primarily recognized for holding a bowl of fruits or vegetables, highlighting its importance in the context of food organization. This counter has been identified as the correct location for the bowl, contrasting with previous instances where it was incorrectly placed.

In addition to housing the bowl, the left counter is intended to accommodate various kitchen utensils, such as spatulas. However, there was an instance where an attempt to place a spatula on the counter was unsuccessful. The left counter is also noted as the destination for transferring a strawberry, further emphasizing its significant role in food organization.

Moreover, the left counter has been associated with the organization of objects, indicated by its connection to a receptacle. It was designated as a target location for a hammer, though the intended movement of this tool proved unsuccessful, resulting in it remaining on a brown table. The left counter has served as the location where an orange was positioned before an attempt to pick it up, as well as being the intended destination for a plum.

Overall, the left counter is a vital piece of furniture within the kitchen, contributing significantly to food preparation and the overall organization of kitchen tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The left counter provides a designated area within the indoor environment for placing items, including the right receptacle mentioned.&lt;SEP&gt;The left counter is positioned off the left edge of the living area and intended to receive objects from elsewhere.</data>
