    <node id="sink">
      <data key="d0">sink</data>
      <data key="d1">receptacle</data>
      <data key="d2">The sink is a versatile fixture primarily used for holding water, essential in both kitchens and bathrooms. It is commonly designed as a basin that facilitates washing or pouring liquids. This specific sink is characterized as a gray or metallic, partially visible structure, often paired with dark countertop materials that enhance both practicality and aesthetic appeal. Typically installed near kitchen counters, the sink features a recessed design that improves functionality for cleaning tasks. It comes in various shapes, with a square design being particularly popular, and serves as an effective solution for washing and cleaning activities in both domestic and commercial environments. The sink is specifically designed for use in cleaning dishes or hands.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"hold;"wash;clean;contain";drain;drain";fill</data>
