    <node id="Perception Update">
      <data key="d0">Perception Update</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"An event indicating an update to the agent's sensory observations in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;Perception Update refers to a significant event type that indicates a change or enhancement in an agent's understanding or awareness of its surrounding environment. This process involves the agent correcting its comprehension of the objects present, which is fundamental for effective interaction and operational effectiveness in various settings, such as a kitchen. 

Perception Updates encompass the observation and recording of environmental contexts that relate to specific tasks, providing vital information necessary for refreshing the current status of these environments or associated objects. Such updates are characterized by a shift in the agent's observations and understanding, thereby refining awareness and ensuring that tasks are informed by accurate and relevant environmental data.

Additionally, Perception Updates may include specific details, such as updates related to the visibility and interaction status of objects, exemplified by the padlock. Overall, they play a crucial role in facilitating more effective interactions with the environment, which ultimately enhances the agent's operational capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"observe;assess"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Perception Update refers to the adjustment in an agent's identification of objects following an initial misidentification, such as that of a red plate. It encompasses the comprehensive process through which an embodied agent records and interprets observations relevant to specific tasks within its environment. This involves accurately identifying locations and objects necessary for transporting items, including recognizing the need to move a padlock based on task requests and handling elements such as legos. 

The Perception Update signifies a substantial change in the agent's processing of information regarding its surroundings, especially after navigating through the environment. It reflects a critical assessment of the spatial layout and various objects present in the room, contributing to a coherent understanding essential for effective task performance. Furthermore, it highlights the status of the environment prior to executing the requested task, indicating a state change or response to ongoing observation activities, particularly in areas such as the kitchen. 

In the context of uncertainty, the Perception Update also suggests doubt regarding the padlock’s location, indicating it may not have been on the table as initially assumed. Moreover, it involves observations made after navigating to specific areas, such as cabinet 5 and the tabletop scene, demonstrating the agent's adaptive capabilities in processing spatial information and object recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;The perception update allows the agent to process its surroundings, particularly near the sofa.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-72ad2634d34d4b3169e1daee0ccd0684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5596398bc39ecae6d2e1945b561210e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36957565c6ea6fce819a9a9c50ac0a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcf85a9b7a90233d118a40b1d62cdbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4920e25d5550d43da37f4ad991763d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd190f719d592d9b0f1509b77990754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f93dfabfba6dc08423e7935263ea5dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310f6849688d33ba61c420abce867dd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc59ff586b37aeb22c2de5df74900a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a560004a654689859efd2f3eb3e3dde2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77091ba04dfe7fcfdc66f950ba9f0d7</data>
