    <node id="Kitchen Counter">
      <data key="d0">Kitchen Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A dark-colored (black/dark gray) kitchen counter where various kitchen objects are arranged."&lt;SEP&gt;The Kitchen Counter is a flat surface typically found in kitchens, primarily used for food preparation and arranging various objects. It is usually designed in a black or dark charcoal-gray color, which adds a modern aesthetic to kitchen environments. This essential workspace facilitates interaction with different kitchen items and supports a variety of tasks related to cooking and food handling. Additionally, the Kitchen Counter often includes features such as drawers and is organized to accommodate various utensils and ingredients, making it a central and multifunctional element in the overall design of a kitchen.&lt;SEP&gt;"A piece of furniture typically used in a kitchen for food preparation and organization."</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The kitchen counter is a vital surface within a kitchen environment, characterized by its dark charcoal-gray surface. It serves not only as a functional workspace but also as a significant focal point where various kitchen items are arranged for efficient access. The counter features a drawer located on its right side, which provides convenient storage for utensils and other essential kitchen tools. As the agent navigates this space, the kitchen counter facilitates interaction with these objects, making it an integral part of culinary tasks and overall kitchen organization. Its design and functionality enhance the spatial dynamics of the kitchen, allowing for an orderly and effective workspace for cooking activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The kitchen counter serves as the observational setting where various kitchen objects are present.&lt;SEP&gt;The kitchen counter is described as having a dark charcoal-gray surface where various objects are arranged.</data>
