    <node id="Right Counter">
      <data key="d0">Right Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">surface</data>
      <data key="d2">The Right Counter is a versatile and functional piece of furniture designed specifically for indoor use, particularly in kitchen environments. It features a polished light brown wooden surface, which provides an essential area for placing and preparing food as well as various other items. Positioned on the right side of the kitchen, the Right Counter serves as a practical workspace for numerous kitchen tasks.

This counter is equipped with two cabinet doors that enhance its storage capabilities, making it a valuable addition to any kitchen setup. The flat, light wood-finished surface offers an organized area where various objects can be easily accessed and utilized. In addition to its utilitarian function, the Right Counter currently displays a collection of Lego items, highlighting its dual purpose as both a workspace and a space for play and creativity.

Furthermore, the design of the Right Counter includes a mounted robotic arm, indicating advanced functionality that may assist with various kitchen operations. Adjustments have been made to the Right Counter's previously recorded location to improve usability, ensuring that it effectively meets the demands of the kitchen environment. Overall, the Right Counter exemplifies a blend of practicality and creativity within its design, establishing itself as an integral component of the kitchen setting.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"hold;"support;"support";"support_items;hold;store";store_objects"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"upper right corner"&lt;SEP&gt;"upper right corner"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The Right Counter is presented with limited specific information, as indicated by the notation "N/A" in three instances. However, it is highlighted that the Right Counter is positioned as "foreground on the right," suggesting its prominent location or visibility within a particular setting. This notable positioning reinforces the importance of the Right Counter in the scene, indicating that it plays a significant role despite the lack of additional details.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Right Counter is a multifunctional surface located in the kitchen area of a living space, distinguished by its light brown wooden finish and polished appearance. This counter serves as a crucial workspace for various operations, particularly food preparation and organizing items such as Lego. Prominently positioned in the foreground of the kitchen, it is a primary area for interaction and task execution.

A key feature of the Right Counter is its role in facilitating operations involving a mounted robotic arm, which is situated above it. This robotic arm aids in completing multiple tasks, making the Right Counter an essential starting point for movements of various kitchen tools. Noteworthy items frequently associated with the Right Counter include a spatula, a Clamp, and occasionally a padlock. For instance, the spatula is often placed on the Right Counter before being used, signifying its importance in the workflow. Similarly, the Clamp is typically set on the Right Counter initially before being transferred to a receptacle on the left counter.

Despite its significance in kitchen operations, organizational challenges can arise related to the Right Counter. There have been instances where items such as a bowl have been misplaced on its surface, and occasions where the counter was expected to contain Lego but instead housed unrelated items. These incidents underscore potential issues with organization within the kitchen space.

In summary, the Right Counter is a vital component of kitchen operations, supporting food preparation, item organization, and the functionality of a robotic arm. It acts as a central location for important kitchen tools like the spatula and Clamp, playing an essential role in facilitating various tasks and managing items within the kitchen environment.</data>
