      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The User is portrayed as the primary actor actively engaged in a variety of tasks not only within the kitchen but also in other environments, demonstrating a hands-on approach to managing different objects. Their responsibilities include initiating and executing actions related to the movement of items, which underscores their active role in ongoing activities.

The User has taken the lead in moving various objects, such as a spatula, and has expressed intentions to move additional items, like a plum from the sofa to the left counter, although this specific action has yet to be carried out. They have made requests to move other objects, including a screwdriver, further emphasizing their proactive engagement in these activities.

In addition to these tasks, the User has initiated the movement of a strawberry and has demonstrated a goal-oriented mindset by requesting the retrieval of a plate from the sink. Their involvement extends to placing a sponge and a ball to the right of the sink, as well as engaging in tasks related to moving a LEGO piece, alongside an unspecified task involving a knife. The User also plays a vital role in correcting and updating memory regarding the spatial information of the kitchen, such as the location of a bowl and the positioning of a red plate.

Overall, the User’s comprehensive engagement in the domestic environment highlights their significance in organizing and executing various activities effectively, ensuring that spatial awareness is accurately maintained while actively managing the items around them.</data>
