      <data key="d1">structure</data>
      <data key="d2">"A set of steps leading to another level."&lt;SEP&gt;The staircase is a construction designed to provide a means of ascending or descending between various levels of a building or structure. It consists of a set of steps that facilitate movement between these levels, effectively allowing passage from one floor to another. This essential architectural feature serves as a critical component in both residential and commercial designs, ensuring accessibility and connectivity within multi-level environments.</data>
